=head1 NAME

qesub - submit job(s) relating to elctronic structure theory (EST) program to SLURM. 

=head1 SYNOPSIS

I<qesub> [ options ] I<infile> 

=head2 Infile:

Four modes are provided:

=over 5

=item 1. I<$infile> = B<filename>; submit single job

=item 2. I<$infile> = 'B<all>'; submit all jobs in the current folder

=item 3. I<$infile> = 'B<fail>'; submit failed jobs

=item 4. I<$infile> = B<*.dat>; submit selected jobs in a list

=back

=head2 Options:

=over 8

=back

=head3

=over 8

=item -h, --help    show this help message and exit

=back

=head3 B<EST related:>

=over 8

=item -e [B<orca|g16|jellyfish>]      assign EST program 

=back

=head3 B<SLURM related:>

=over 8

=item -np B<procs>  invoke a parallel job with B<procs> cpus.

=item -p B<partition>    specify the SLURM partition.

=item -t B<time>    specify the time limit for the job (format: HH:MM:SS).

=back

=head1 EXAMPLES

 Submit an ORCA job with 1 core (Minimum Syntax):
 ]$ qesub molecule.inp 

 Submit an ORCA job with 8 cores:
 ]$ qesub -np 8 molecule.inp 

 Submit all the jobs in the current directory: 
 ]$ qesub all 

